t 12, Lauderdale County has a rain record on 6 grids from 1951 to 2025, and October to November came in under 90% of normal in 38 of those 75 years on the middle of the grids. In 2025, July to August came in at 31% of normal and November to December at 35% on the middle. In 2026 so far, January to February sat at 40% of normal on the middle, and every grid&rsquo;s driest year was 1963, as low as 57% on grid 19061.</p>"}
